{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"1a4181f2f4ca7039","type":"text","text":"## Follicular phase\n- FSH stimulates primordial follicle -> tertiary follicles\n- These produce oestrogen and inhibin B\n- The singular dominant follicle secretes oestrogen","x":-999,"y":110,"width":379,"height":210},
		{"id":"047de65cf44664d5","x":-1600,"y":396,"width":380,"height":208,"type":"text","text":"## Proliferative phase\n- Oestrogen causes increased endometrial growth and vascular innervation \n- Cervical mucus secretions start to be modified"},
		{"id":"688c88c7e7868a81","type":"text","text":"Dominant follicle doesn't degenerate bc FSH stimulates the production of additional FSH receptors within it -> increased sensitivity even as FSH levels decline \nFSH also induces development of LH receptors inside the dominant follicle","x":-865,"y":829,"width":420,"height":209},
		{"id":"cc89edbe9b539519","type":"text","text":"Negative feedback of inhibin B/oestrogen with FSH causes the non-dominant follicles to degenerate","x":-1099,"y":494,"width":359,"height":220},
		{"id":"a875b89834294e90","x":-480,"y":340,"width":392,"height":220,"type":"text","text":"- Oestrogen levels have been rising steadily... somehow. Reaches a threshold -> induces a switch from negative to positive feedback loop with the APG\n\t- APG expresses more GnRH receptors \n\t- Surge of LH secretion (x10) + smaller rise in FSH "},
		{"id":"48d21eabfb368a9f","x":60,"y":560,"width":396,"height":220,"type":"text","text":"# Ovulation! \n- Rupture of follicle -> release of oocyte ~36-44 hours after LH surge - follicle becomes corpus luteum \n- Cervical mucus secretion modification continues -> increased amount of watery mucus"},
		{"id":"b0e48ab679a893f7","type":"text","text":"# Phase 1 ","x":-919,"y":-80,"width":151,"height":71},
		{"id":"632707ad713a75ca","x":-1018,"y":-240,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"# Day 1 - 14"},
		{"id":"b195d34364c6d86f","x":600,"y":-80,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"# Phase 2"},
		{"id":"9bf21dfeeb11423b","x":561,"y":-265,"width":250,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"# Day 15 - 28"},
		{"id":"ab3cb2ebb974cf28","x":725,"y":117,"width":275,"height":60,"type":"text","text":"Progesterone levels increase"}
	],
